Z||000000||chris6878||08-10-2000||11:21 PM||||My headlight motor was continually running in both directions.. up and down.. i replaced the plastic gear with metal gear... but it still does the same, goes up and down... but still runs... what else could i check?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||08-11-2000||08:41 AM||||What year model car is it?  If it is an 84 thru 86 it could be the limit switches are bad.  This is a mechanical switch inside the motor housing.  It is accessed through a small rectangular (about 1" x 2" secured by three screws) cover plate on the side of the motor.  If it is the newer model the limit stops are controlled electronically.<P>Try this link for info from Oliver Scholz:<P>wysiwyg://main.45http://www.frank.../users/dagobah/luke/headlight.html<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
